  "summary": "An orifice plate flowmeter is a thin plate with a precise sharp-edged hole clamped between two flanges. The restriction speeds the flow up and lowers its pressure; the pressure difference between upstream and downstream taps is measured by a DP transmitter, and the flow rate is proportional to the square root of that difference (ISO 5167-2). Simple, cheap and standardised, but with a high permanent pressure loss.",
  "classification": {
    "family": "Differential-pressure flowmeter",
    "type": "Concentric square-edged orifice, flange taps"
  },
